    <!-- CORE PHILOSOPHY -->
    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="space-y-12">

          <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
            <div>
              <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Person-centred practice</h2>
              <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Every individual is unique. The same diagnosis can create entirely different experiences in two different people. That's why instead of standard "prescriptions," we offer a process developed together with each client.</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">A psychologist may be an expert; but the only expert on your own life is you. We simply accompany you in discovering that expertise.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-8 border border-warm-tertiary">
              <blockquote class="font-serif text-lg text-ink leading-relaxed italic">
                "No two clients are the same — and neither are any two sessions."
              </blockquote>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
            <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-primary/15 lg:order-1">
              <blockquote class="font-serif text-lg text-ink leading-relaxed italic">
                "Being evidence-based means following new research and bringing it into practice."
              </blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="lg:order-2">
              <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Science and intuition together</h2>
              <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">We apply scientifically validated methods such as CBT, psychodynamic therapy and ACT. But we use these methods flexibly according to each client's needs — we don't mechanically apply rigid protocols.</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Balancing both the research agenda and clinical intuition is the key to effective therapy.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
            <div>
              <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Trauma-informed care</h2>
              <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Trying to "change" someone without first understanding why they behave as they do doesn't work. Together, we understand the experiences, wounds and defences behind behaviours.</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">A safe therapeutic relationship is a prerequisite for working through trauma.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-accent/5 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-accent/15">
              <blockquote class="font-serif text-lg text-ink leading-relaxed italic">
                "There is always meaning behind behaviour."
              </blockquote>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- APPROACHES -->
    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
          <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-3">The approaches we use</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted max-w-lg mx-auto text-sm">Not one model, but multiple frameworks integrated according to each client's needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 text-sm">Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">A structured, goal-focused approach for recognising thought patterns and replacing them with more functional ones.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 text-sm">Psychodynamic Therapy</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">An in-depth approach that explores unconscious processes and early relationship patterns to create lasting change.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 text-sm">Acceptance &amp; Commitment Therapy (ACT)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">An approach centred on accepting rather than suppressing emotions and living in line with personal values.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 text-sm">Systemic Therapy</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">A framework that views the individual within their family, relationships and environment; commonly used in family therapy.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 text-sm">Mindfulness-Based Approaches</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Techniques that strengthen emotional regulation and reduce stress and anxiety through conscious awareness practice.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

